  }]], "2ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"6748387a-5e89-46fd-93a4-\
512fc527ffb3"],

Cell["\<\
The underlying algebra is the free graded commutative algebra on the \
generators: a generator of even degree is polynomial, and one of odd degree \
squares to zero.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"dac790c6-eec1-4c0c-a4b0-53d94fb04443"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A monomial is written as a product of generators and is read in the order \
the model declares them, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"x", " ", "y"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "79fa479a-681a-4e16-b118-d2192b2e2bd6"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"y", " ", "x"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "91834c07-0e1d-4ce5-97ef-949e1541050e"],
 " are the same expression and denote the same monomial. The sign of a \
reordering is produced by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["SullivanModelProduct"]], 
    "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/SullivanModelProduct", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "7a90d0be-cef8-4efd-b8d7-54d9713d5ab3"],
 ", not by the way a monomial is typed."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e9f3dca3-9b0c-4562-bb81-536da141c7a2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["orientation", "TI"],
 " is either a monomial of degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bdfd23c5-0fbd-43d4-be45-20ba188eb914"],
 ", meaning the functional that is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["1", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6a101e7b-dc14-4949-a74f-2b4e3cd50bed"],
 " on it and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "de93f922-6f3e-4b7c-8ba6-fdb1482f2d3a"],
 " on the other monomials of degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "760e6f93-2836-4b10-9e2c-e2b20041a028"],
 ", or an Association of numeric values on monomials of degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e98756d3-2c3b-4166-862c-56d3e4cf81e7"],
 ". Zero values are dropped."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d5036512-6f5d-447e-8825-befe7a56b274"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The orientation must be one in the sense of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["OrientationQ"]], "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/OrientationQ", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "cd502b89-d158-4c22-b96e-bde2a940cde7"],
 ": it vanishes on the image of the differential and is nonzero on some \
cocycle of degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "87b44b5a-8fd3-4e7e-b875-5f1652f44dbb"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"977eda2d-a4e7-4c94-b52f-d2f0c58e79f8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The result is a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Failure"]], "paclet:ref/Failure"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "2d638fba-4073-4cad-b40b-9c206c9fcaef"],
 " when the differential does not raise the degree by one or does not square \
to zero, and when the values do not define an orientation."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"15adeda8-e861-4dcf-8487-ce8edb3dc210"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The default generator symbols are created in the current context: ",
 Cell[BoxData["v"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "abc54802-d019-4369-9ee3-76138904dfa4"],
 " for the circle, ",
 Cell[BoxData["a"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "873c02b2-cdf8-4e9e-afea-bdc263bb5b96"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["b"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "60b86b28-629a-4f8d-b365-200510eec743"],
 " for a projective space, ",
 Cell[BoxData["x"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f72071cf-7901-4934-876f-0d47f374ef49"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["y"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d4fb46f0-d93a-4192-8d42-797b79948980"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["z"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3dc41ce6-2f64-4cc1-a08d-0ebfeeb26c45"],
 " for the Heisenberg nilmanifold, and so on. ",
 StyleBox["generators", "TI"],
 " chooses them, which is also how a collision is avoided when two models are \
tensored."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e486eab4-2a29-4d8b-9abf-0222a767e975"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["truncation", "TI"],
 " is an integer, or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Infinity"]], "paclet:ref/Infinity"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "c17894db-cb9e-462a-8962-54ccfa32757c"],
 " for no truncation, the default. The monomials above any degree span a \
differential graded ideal, since the differential raises the degree by one, \
so the quotient is again a differential graded algebra."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"bc83138b-c523-4d4d-bf1b-9db12c525d83"],

Cell["\<\
In a tensor product the generators of the factors must be disjoint. The \
differentials and the truncations are joined, the orientations multiplied and \
the degrees added; each truncation stays with the generators of its factor.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"8fc1eb3d-55f8-43ae-bc49-95eaf7531c7d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Input of another shape returns unevaluated: a generator of degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bfd790f9-e34c-49e8-96f9-58a92087739b"],
 ", a differential that is not a polynomial in the generators, a non-numeric \
orientation value, a tensor product whose factors share a generator, a \
catalogue parameter out of range."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"943a2bae-8388-4129-880a-b617a3e5eb0c"]
}, Open  ]],

